{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/181249-tribes-being-auspices-problem","id":181249,"title":"\"Tribes being Auspices\" problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T14:40:12-07:00","id":181249,"title":"\"Tribes being Auspices\" problem","content":"One of bigger things I have problem with <b>Forsaken</b> setting is that most Tribes are working as &quot;second Auspice&quot; for character. Blood Talons are basically Rahu, Bone Shadows are Ithaeur, Iron Masters are Irraka, etc. Worse, they can be chosen for double role, so the Blood Talons Rahu is what? Most Rahu of Rahus? And Iron Masters Irraka is as such secretive, it can't be found?<br /> <br /> It get to me when my players were choosing Tribes for they characters. Most choose just Tribe that is like &quot;second Auspice&quot; of they PC, the same they have. It could be even to overcome, if Renown weren't also connected with Tribes as &quot;second Auspice&quot;. Of course Storm Lords are having Honor, because Elodoth have them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know the Favorites Preys are add in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> to Tribes to help mitigate this, but I still see it, and somehow it made me cringe on this part of setting. Other game lines have they X-Splat and Y-Splat totally unconnected, so characters are more interesting. In Werewolf it looks... well, a bit dull. You can be &quot;super Rahu&quot;, &quot;super Ithaeur&quot; and a like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:47:03-07:00","id":181264,"title":"","content":"To think that auspice is the same as tribe is to misunderstand a crucial part of the setting. Tribes can be chosen. No werewolf choses his auspice. A Rahu is a person imbued with the destiny of a killer. He might not like it. He might even struggle with his auspice. He might eventually come to terms with it, or not. The auspice cannot be changed. A Blood Talon makes the intentional choice to emulate the destroyer wolf and to live by his Code. His is a choice, one that can be reverted. To confuse the two is to misunderstand the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:53:22-07:00","id":181271,"title":"","content":"That isn't actually a counterargument to what wyrdhamster is saying. It's tangengical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:05:14-07:00","id":181278,"title":"","content":"I think the argument also falls down very quickly when you look at it a bit more closely.<br /> <br /> If you go just by concept, the Blood Talons and Bone Shadows are the only ones that really have an issue with significant overlap. Blood Talons and Rahu overlap in their focus on fighting, and Bone Shadows and Ithaeur overlap by being focused on spirits. The other three Tribes don't have any particular focus based issue.<br /> <br /> If you look at the mechanics (aka the overlap of Renown) things do not line up.<br /> <br /> Combine the two and there's actually plenty of differences. And the books have put some decent page count into expanding on this in supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:14:13-07:00","id":181286,"title":"","content":"And that's a proper counter argument. Though as you say, Blood Talons and Bone Shadows do have a problem here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I am mostly disatisfied with the Auspices but for a completely different reason. I feel they're too close to &quot;what you do&quot; instead of &quot;what you are&quot;. Now (AFAIK) a Warrior or Shaman could very well be &quot;what you are&quot;, but us post-industrial gamers typically don't have the cultural context for that and I don't feel the books (or Werewolf's Tier 1 focus) was sufficient to bridge the divide.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather the Auspices were different archetypes of Werewolf, like Clans are different archetypes of Vampires. But maybe the Idgiam Chronicles will fix the missing cultural context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:57:46-07:00","id":181409,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the Blood Talons have a particular issue when you combine the fluff and mechanics side of things. Consider that Blood Talons have Glory as their Renown, and Rahu have Purity. Those are two very different lenses to view &quot;fighting&quot; with.<br /> <br /> As well, the Bone Shadows don't actually have a clean line up to the Ithaeur. The Ithaeur ritual focus is one way to deal with spirits, but the Elodoth Auspice ability is just as much in-line with the Bone Shadow philosophy.<br /> <br /> Again, when you combine fluff and mechanics, things become more divergent. The &quot;overlap&quot; is more of not taking a closer look than it is a real problem with the game. And even more so from the IC previews.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> The problem with archetypes was Auspices is... well, there isn't the same proliferation of werewolf archetypes as their are vampire archetypes that really fit into the same mold.<br /> <br /> Most different &quot;types&quot; or werewolves on a genre level are more about why/how a werewolf came into existence. Which doesn't really gel well was a single type of player character group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T19:07:04-07:00","id":181512,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with Tribes being re-focused on &quot;what you hunt&quot; and Auspices being re-focused on &quot;how you hunt&quot; I see this being even less of an issue post-IC. There's no reason werewolves would be any more appropriate of a prey for warrior-hunters than spirits are, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:22:08-07:00","id":181922,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always found it\u2019s easy to get past this issue by breaking them down to the essentials.<br /> <br /> The Auspices are the traditional tribal roles:<br /> Rahu \u2013 warrior, fighter, protector<br /> Cahalith \u2013 storyteller, lore keeper, artist<br /> Elodoth \u2013 advisor, elder of the tribe, councilman<br /> Ithaeur \u2013 shaman, healer, wise man<br /> Irraka \u2013 hunter, thief, spy<br /> <br /> The Tribes are based on wolf/werewolf symbolism:<br /> 1) Storm Lords are The Wolf as Protector/Ruler. Romulus and Remus owe their lives to a she-wolf, as does little Mowgli, so that one is fairly wide-spread. Many a king claimed to dream of wolves, be safe in the company of wolves, or be part wolf themselves.<br /> 2) Blood Talons are The Wolf as Hunter/Warrior. The wolf-skin warriors all over Indo-European myths, several Arctic tribes revered wolves. This one is so common it doesn\u2019t really need explanation.<br /> 3) Hunters in Darkness are The Wolf as Devourer/Predator. The above is the positive spin; this one is the negative spin, which is also quite common. The Big Bad Wolf being the number 1 example, closely followed by Fenris. The Fear of the Darkness made manifest.<br /> 4) Iron Masters are The Wolf as Companion/Partner. This is that middle ground between becoming the loyal dog and continuing to be the wild animal. Tame enough to protect what is considered \u201ctheir property\u201d but still wild enough to be dangerous.<br /> 5) Bone Shadows are The Wolf as Omen/Death. One of the lesser known ones, mostly in Native American myths, but there are a few that place dogs/wolves as guardians of the Underworld or psychopomps guiding people (or taking them by force) to the lands of the dead.<br /> <br /> The Auspice is the natural skills and tendencies they're born with. The Tribe is how they choose to apply those skills and tendencies they've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 06-27-2014, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:30:36-07:00","id":181927,"title":"","content":"Tribes are chosen. Auspices are chosen for you by something outside your control. This hard distinction mandates different play styles, different archetypes and different playing experiences.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> Rahu are born warriors and killers, <i>whether they like it or not</i>.<br /> Blood Talons choose, <i>intentionally, purposefully</i>, for some or other reason, to live as killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:26:44-07:00","id":181980,"title":"","content":"I like the new Idigam Chronicle definitions of Tribes, which make things much clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:57:50-07:00","id":182067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/181249-tribes-being-auspices-problem?p=181409#post181409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with archetypes was Auspices is... well, there isn't the same proliferation of werewolf archetypes as their are vampire archetypes that really fit into the same mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about this. We had some good discussions and ideas on the old forums, and it's ok to add a new archetype to fill out the numbers if they fit alongside the old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T10:51:04-07:00","id":182103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/181249-tribes-being-auspices-problem?p=181512#post181512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, with Tribes being re-focused on &quot;what you hunt&quot; and Auspices being re-focused on &quot;how you hunt&quot; I see this being even less of an issue post-IC. There's no reason werewolves would be any more appropriate of a prey for warrior-hunters than spirits are, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it makes the tribes actually feel sensible to be in the setting with the hunt focus ^^<br /> <br /> As for the focus on different aspects of werewolves, let's list them and see how Forsaken includes them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves as Cursed (New Wolf-Blooded, Ghost wolves)<br /> Werewolves as deals with the Devil/malicious spirit (Bale Hounds)<br /> Werewolves as split personalities (Zi'ir, new Haromy highs)<br /> Werewolves as protectors (Hunters in the Darkness, Storm Lords)<br /> Werewolves as mindless killers (Kuruth, Gauru form)<br /> Werewolves as God's own (Any Christian lodge)<br /> <br /> I think there are few more, but I'm rather derp atm XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T11:23:29-07:00","id":182119,"title":"","content":"There's a looooot more aspects, but to expound on them would be to spoil several lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T01:09:00-07:00","id":184652,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the problem tends to be peoples over simplification of the status' in general. Reading signs of the moon and tribes of the moon dispels that pretty damn quick. Instead of focusing on blood talon as rahu, focus on them being the blunt &quot;fuck this noise&quot; types. Instead of bone shadows being spirit workers, consider them an overly curious folk with spectral shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T16:21:24-07:00","id":185833,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think the tribes act as a guiding point for how you choose to follow your auspices, rather than acting as a second auspice itself.<br /> <br /> For example, the shaman role. If they joined the Bone Shadows, they'd probably take on the role of being a wiseman or a spiritual leader of the People. If they joined the Blood Talons, they might become a witchdoctor, riling up the spirits and turning them against their enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> The role of the warrior could also be changed depending on their tribe. Sure if you joined the Blood Talons, you could be a savage barbarian, but if you joined the Hunters in Darkness, you could be a deadly assassin, or a trained commando if you joined the Iron Masters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tribes should be treated as a way of life for your character, not simply treating them like a power boost. If all you focus on is the bonuses, you'll never be able to fully immerse yourself in the game, it becomes a power play at that point, as opposed to role playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}